On 6 Feb., 06:08, purple arcanist <ejg_...@yahoo.com> wrote:
> Please post the times you have gotten the Book of the Dead, with
> Rodney still alive and no use of wizard mode, for style.

I've done that a couple of times. You have several options how to
engineer this. Most involve wearing a ring of free action and hitting
the guy with a potion of paralysis. It is a good idea to check each
turn with a stethoscope if he is still paralyzed.

1) You can polyself into a nymph and steal the book.

2) You can level-drain him (Stormbringer/staff only) until your pet
nymph attacks him.

3) You can level-teleport up his tower. If the uppermost level has not
yet been created, you have a chance of landing on his spot. Do this
with autopickup.


What does not work:
4) You can dig a corner of his tower without waking him up. Speed
boots occasionally give you two turns in a row. Sadly, you cannot jump
on the first free turn and paralyze him on the second one.

5) The same thing goes for walking right next to him as a xorn.

6) In theory, you could also feed your pet nymph enough potions of
gain level so it will attack him without external aid. (Conflict is
not enough: a nymph is too low-level to hit.)

7) Finally, if you paralyze the guy before he pick the book up, you
could teleport both, cast detect treasure, and try to get the book
before he does. This almost never works outside wizard mode.

Now, the big challenge is: If you are playing a neutral pacifist
atheist polyself-less polypile-less wishless weaponless genocideless
wizard, is there a semi-reliable way to get The Book without killing
the Wizard?


